From 29d515fe090580789046650281bc9bfa9bf1cdcb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 04:01:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] llama: a second scheduler for the MTP draft context's graphs
 with outputs (LLAMA_DRAFT_SCHED2)

The draft context alternates a no-output ingest graph and a 1-token draft-step graph every cycle.  Graph reuse needs
the scheduler's split/allocation state to belong to the graph, so with one scheduler both were rebuilt every cycle
(~0.5 ms host, mostly ggml_backend_sched_alloc_graph).  The graphs with outputs now run on a second scheduler that is
swapped into `sched` for the duration of a decode/encode, so both graphs stay allocated and are reused.

The meta (tensor-split) backend keeps the external views of a buffer in a rotating pair of containers that assumes one
live graph; a rebuild cleared the views of the other graph (GGML_ASSERT(bcj.nodes[i]) in graph_compute).  Each
scheduler now selects its own view slot (ggml_backend_meta_set_view_slot), with its own rotating pair.

LLAMA_DRAFT_SCHED2=0 restores the single scheduler.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
